robin wrote:
> OK, the patch works great but for reasons I absolutely  cannot fathom
> it's breaking saved game compatibility.  We can't deploy a patch that
> does that during the tournament.

Hm, with a bit of hackery, this might not be such a big problem, I
suspect.

For each server:
0) At some point before rolling out the change, ensure each server has
an updated binary present, but not replacing the old one.
1) Set the server to down so no one can start an old-version game but
miss being flagged.
2) Flag anyone who has a savefile or a currently running game by some
means. Creating an empty file of their name in an appropriate directory
is probably easiest, although for future-proofing perhaps the file
should contain an identifier for the patch version in case more than
one old version needs to be present at once.
3) Alter the login script so that at the end of the script, instead of
starting nethack, it checks to see if they have an old-savefile flag.
   a) If they don't, start the new binary.
   b) If they do, check to see if they actually have a savefile or any
recover files.
      i) If they do, start the old binary.
      ii) If they don't, remove their flag, then start the new binary.
4) Set the server to up.

Assuming step 3 is prepared and tested in advance, this could actually
be relatively quick and painless, which is I suppose the first sign to
me that I've missed something and this won't work. I'd love to try to
act wise about any other problems this would create, though, too ;)

